  "title": "Braille letters - EEG",
  "description": "Raw EEG recordings from participants who received tactile Braille letters (B, C, D, L, M, N, V, Z) on Braille cells under the left and right index fingers. The dataset accompanies a study on how sensory representations are transformed into perceptual Braille letter representations in the visually deprived brain. Data are provided in BrainVision format with event files describing trial onsets, stimulus types, catch trials and pedal responses.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with BrainVision equipment while Braille letters were presented tactually to the left or right index finger. Triggers coded letter identity and hand, trial and stimulus onsets, catch trials, and pedal presses. Some recordings were split into multiple runs, and some participants completed a second session.",
